messages:
tara: opened a small PR to add a 'paginated streaming' pattern to the SDK snippets. goal: show how to iterate pages where each page returns a resumable stream, persist resume tokens per page, and dedupe on resume. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5120 :page_with_curl:

ben: nice. can you show the lifecycle: open page stream -> process chunks -> on transient error resume the same page stream -> dedupe duplicates? that's the common confusion i see in support.

tara: yup. i added compact examples for python/ts/go and a few one-liners about why small batches help interactive latency. core rules in the doc: 1) persist resume_token per page, 2) record last_sequence_id per page, 3) when resuming, pass the same kv_cache_hint and ignore sequence ids <= last_sequence_id to dedupe.

tara: python snippet (illustrative):
```python
# python - paginated streaming pattern (sketch)
page_token = None
state = {}  # map page_token -> { resume_token, last_seq }
while True:
    # request a page, which returns a resumable stream
    with client.stream_page("gpt-4o-mini", page_token=page_token, batch_size=3, kv_cache_hint="corpus:42") as s:
        try:
            for chunk in s:
                seq = chunk.get("seq")  # monotonic per-page seq id
                if seq <= state.get(page_token, {}).get("last_seq", -1):
                    continue  # dedupe resumed payloads
                process_chunk(chunk)
                # persist progress for this page
                state.setdefault(page_token, {})["last_seq"] = seq
                state[page_token]["resume_token"] = chunk.get("resume_token")
        except TransientError:
            # on transient error, resume using persisted token for this page
            resume = state[page_token]["resume_token"]
            s.resume(resume)  # SDK should accept resume token and kv cache
    # get next page_token from the last response (or break)
    page_token = s.final_page_token
    if not page_token:
        break
```

ben: good. one nit: show explicit persist (db) comment for production.

tara: added comment: "persist state to durable storage (DB) between attempts".

zoe: added TS example showing paginate + per-page stream and dedupe logic:
```ts
// typescript - combining paginate + per-page stream
let pageToken: string | null = null
const progress: Record<string, { resumeToken?: string; lastSeq?: number }> = {}
while (true) {
  const page = await client.fetchPage('gpt-4o-mini', { pageToken, pageSize: 30 })
  const s = await client.streamPage('gpt-4o-mini', { pageToken: page.token, batchSize: 3, kvCacheHint: 'corpus:42' })
  try {
    for await (const chunk of s) {
      const seq = chunk.seq
      if (seq <= (progress[page.token]?.lastSeq ?? -1)) continue
      handleChunk(chunk)
      progress[page.token] = { resumeToken: chunk.resumeToken, lastSeq: seq }
      // persist progress[page.token] to storage if needed
    }
  } catch (err) {
    // on transient failure: resume with stored token for this page
    const resume = progress[page.token]?.resumeToken
    if (resume) await s.resume(resume)
  } finally {
    await s.close()
  }
  if (!page.nextToken) break
  pageToken = page.nextToken
}
```

tara: and a Go sketch with jittered backoff + resume call.
```go
// go - paginated streaming sketch
var pageToken string
progress := map[string]struct{ resume string; lastSeq int }{}
for {
  page, _ := client.FetchPage("gpt-4o-mini", PageOpts{Token: pageToken, Size:30})
  s, _ := client.StreamPage("gpt-4o-mini", StreamOpts{PageToken: page.Token, BatchSize:3, KVCacheHint:"corpus:42"})
  defer s.Close()
  for {
    chunk, err := s.Recv()
    if err == io.EOF { break }
    if err != nil {
      time.Sleep(jitter(retries))
      // try to resume using saved token
      if p, ok := progress[page.Token]; ok {
        s.Resume(p.resume)
      }
      continue
    }
    if chunk.Seq <= progress[page.Token].lastSeq { continue }
    process(chunk)
    progress[page.Token] = struct{ resume string; lastSeq int }{resume: chunk.ResumeToken, lastSeq: chunk.Seq}
  }
  if page.NextToken == "" { break }
  pageToken = page.NextToken
}
```

ben: love the explicit dedupe by seq id. maybe also add one-sentence guidance on batch_size default: "use batch_size=3-4 for interactive paginated streams; raise to 8+ for large bulk pages."

tara: added that. also added a one-liner: "When resuming any page stream, pass the resume_token and the same kv_cache_hint to avoid duplicated context."

